write: {"path": "findings.json", "content": "{
  "categories": [
    {
      "category": "late_count",
      "finding": "In request(), the usage counter is appended to `attempts` only AFTER client.post() completes successfully. Budget accounting is therefore delayed: any concurrent caller checking remaining() while a request is in flight sees a stale count, and failed requests (OSError path) are never counted at all, so LIMIT can be exceeded.",
      "location": "budget.py lines 8-11"
    },
    {
      "category": "local_timezone",
      "finding": "The date stamp uses datetime.now(), i.e. the machine's local timezone, rather than a UTC-aware timestamp (datetime.now(timezone.utc)). Around midnight the recorded date depends on host TZ, producing inconsistent day bucketing across environments.",
      "location": "budget.py line 10"
    },
    {
      "category": "incomplete_price_check",
      "finding": "free_metadata() only inspects 'prompt' and 'completion' keys and treats missing keys as 0 via .get(..., 0). A model entry missing those keys (or carrying other priced components) is silently classified as free, so the price check is incomplete and can misclassify paid models as free.",
      "location": "budget.py lines 15-16"
    },
    {
      "category": "paid_fallback",
      "finding": "fallback() strips the ':free' suffix, yielding the corresponding PAID model name. Falling back this way silently routes traffic to a billable endpoint, a direct paid-request risk.",
      "location": "budget.py lines 18-19"
    },
    {
      "category": "unhealthy_remaining",
      "finding": "remaining() derives headroom purely from len(attempts) and ignores the `healthy` flag entirely (`healthy` is initialized but never read or updated). When the service is unhealthy, remaining() still reports full quota, so callers get a misleading budget figure.",
      "location": "budget.py lines 5, 21-22"
    }
  ]
}
"}
